    "q-183376": {
      "dom_id": "step-q183376",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "For the universal set $U,$ given by\n\n$$\nU={5,10,15,20,25,30,35},\n$$\n\nfind the truth set of $P(x)⇔Q(x)$ for the following predicates: \n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is odd.\n\n- $Q(x):$ $\\sqrt{x}$ is integer.",
      "worked_solution": "Since we have that\n\n$$\nP(x)⇔Q(x)≡(P(x)∧Q(x))∨(¬P(x)∧¬Q(x)),\n$$\n\nthe corresponding truth set can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇔Q}=({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that:\n\n- The truth set of $P(x)$ is \n\n$$\n{T}_{P}={5,15,25,35}\n$$\n\nand its complement is\n\n$$\n{\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}={10,20,30}.\n$$\n\n- The truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n\n$$\n{T}_{Q}={25}\n$$\n\n \nand its complement is\n\n$$\n{\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}={5,10,15,20,30,35}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q} & ={5,15,25,35}\\cap {25} \\\\  & ={25} \\\\ {\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q} & ={10,20,30}\\cap {5,10,15,20,30,35} \\\\  & ={10,20,30} \\\\ {T}_{P⇔Q} & =({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}) \\\\  & ={25}\\cup {10,20,30} \\\\  & ={10,20,25,30}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
